{
  "_comment": "Structures: buildings, defences and fortifications. footprint in tiles [width, depth]; power: + produced, - used; role: what it provides (yard builds structures, barracks trains infantry, factory builds vehicles, post trains levy infantry, warehouse builds supply trucks, fuel is the strategic fuel depot, office is the logistics office that goes up on a captured logistics point); buildRadius: tiles around it where its side may build; cover: % less damage for infantry standing in it; coverAround: same for infantry next to it; blocks: which movement types it stops (default all). Faction 'neutral' structures are civilian buildings: nobody builds them, nobody attacks them unless ordered to, and infantry beside them take cover. garrison: how many infantry it holds (they take half damage inside). income: supplies per minute. perYard: how many of it a side may have for each construction yard it owns. aura: {radius in tiles, fireRate in percent}: friendly units that near fire that much faster. convoy: supply trucks a logistics office runs (it arrives with them: freeUnit); a truck's capacity is what each brings per trip.",
